# each of the two ways of weigh() that call is a framed part of its own, and they meet in a block that the head of neither stands above: every edge into it comes out of a framed part.
# holder lies in a callee-saved register on both. The edges move it to another register, ahead of the teardown, so the block holds nothing that asks for the frame,
# and the two ways that return at once set up none
# f3 = weigh
# REQUIRES: x86_64 unsanitized-code
# RUN: allocate f3:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: unit f3:Body
# CHECK: usedCalleeSaves =
# CHECK: headOfFramedPart =
# CHECK: headOfFramedPart =
# CHECK-NOT: needsFrameAheadOfFramedPart
# RUN(FRAME): frame f3:Body mechanisms=all
# FRAME-LABEL: unit f3:Body
# FRAME: coverage = FramedPart
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell
